crtsys provides CMake helpers and Visual Studio/MSBuild driver-model UI.

CMake:

  find_package(crtsys CONFIG REQUIRED)
  crtsys_add_driver(my_driver src/main.cpp)

Visual Studio/MSBuild manifest projects must use a static-CRT triplet, run
vcpkg install once, and import the installed bridge from Directory.Build.targets
or the .vcxproj. For a repository-local manifest installation:

  <Import
    Project="$([MSBuild]::NormalizePath('$(VcpkgManifestRoot)', 'vcpkg_installed', '$(VcpkgTriplet)', 'share', 'crtsys', 'msbuild', 'crtsys-vcpkg.targets'))"
    Condition="Exists('$([MSBuild]::NormalizePath('$(VcpkgManifestRoot)', 'vcpkg_installed', '$(VcpkgTriplet)', 'share', 'crtsys', 'msbuild', 'crtsys-vcpkg.targets'))')" />

Reload Visual Studio after the first install so the crtsys WDM/KMDF entry-point
property page is reevaluated. See share/crtsys/readme.md for driver examples.
